Package: pve-storage-cetrafs
Architecture: all
Depends: libpve-storage-perl (>= 9.0), ${misc:Depends}, ${perl:Depends}
Recommends: cetrafs-dkms, cetrafs-tools
Description: Proxmox VE storage plugin for the cetrafs clustered filesystem
 cetrafs is a clustered, shared-disk Linux filesystem: several nodes mount
 one shared block device (an iSCSI or FC LUN) at the same time, with VM disk
 images living directly on the one volume, the way VMFS backs vSphere.
 .
 This package adds a 'cetrafs' storage type to Proxmox VE, which mounts the
 shared volume on every node and exposes it as shared storage for VM images,
 container volumes, ISOs, templates and backups.

Package: pve-storage-cetrafs-ui
Architecture: all
Section: admin
Depends: pve-manager (>= 9.0), pve-storage-cetrafs (= ${binary:Version}), ${misc:Depends}
Description: Proxmox VE web UI integration for cetrafs storage (optional)
 Adds the 'cetrafs' storage type to the Proxmox VE web interface:
 Datacenter -> Storage -> Add -> CetraFS, and editing existing cetrafs
 storages. Without it the storage works the same but is managed with pvesm
 and listed as "Unknown" in the web UI.
 .
 pve-manager has no UI plugin interface, so this package adds a script tag to
 /usr/share/pve-manager/index.html.tpl and re-adds it whenever pve-manager is
 upgraded. Removing the package removes the tag.
